<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Philip (missionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Philip was a Scottish missionary who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 1819. He campaigned for the legal rights of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoekhoe">Khoikhoi</a>, and his Researches in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> of 1828, with lobbying in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, helped secure <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordinance-50">Ordinance 50</a> and its confirmation by the British government. Settlers regarded him as a dangerous agitator.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-philip-missionary.jpg" alt="John Philip (missionary)" width="320" height="550" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Thomson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Revd._John_Philip_D.D_(4669882).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
